   "source": [
    "## Using REGCOIL Algorithm for initial guess"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Instead of starting from a circular coilset, we can do a sort of \"warm-start\" by first solving a simpler problem where we find a surface current on an exterior surface which minimizes the normal field error. This problem can be quickly solved as a regularized least-squares problem ([See the REGCOIL tutorial notebook for more info](./coil_optimization_REGCOIL.ipynb)), which can give an initial guess coilset which has low Bn from which to further refine with filamentary coil optimization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from desc.magnetic_fields import (\n",
    "    solve_regularized_surface_current,\n",
    "    FourierCurrentPotentialField,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from scipy.constants import mu_0\n",
    "eq=eq.copy()\n",
    "## First, make a constant-offset surface upon which our surface current will lie.\n",
    "#surface = eq.get_surface_at(rho=0.8)\n",
    "surf = eq.surface.constant_offset_surface(\n",
    "    offset=0.13,  # desired offset (m)\n",
    "    M=16,  # Poloidal resolution of desired offset surface\n",
    "    N=eq.N,  # Toroidal resolution of desired offset surface\n",
    "    grid=LinearGrid(M=36, N=2 * eq.N, NFP=eq.NFP),\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
